@page "/e2e/gantt-v3"
@using System.Text.Json
@using Lumeo.GanttV3
@using Lumeo.Tests.ServerHost.E2E
@using Lumeo.Services

@* Gantt v2/v3 parity harness (feat/gantt-v3, T4) — v3 counterpart of
   GanttV2Page.razor. Renders the working-name GanttChart against the IDENTICAL
   fixture + params (Height/GroupBy/BarColor) so every DOM measurement taken
   here has a like-for-like v2 baseline. See GanttV2Page.razor's remarks for
   the ?fixture / ?viewMode query params.

   Phase 2, T4 (drag parity suite) additions:
   - ?readonly=1 -> GanttChart.Readonly (shared with v2's ?readonly=1).
   - ?allowCreate=1 -> GanttChart.AllowCreate (v3-only; REUI parity, no v2 equivalent).
   - ?candrop=1 -> wires a CanDrop predicate that rejects any proposed drag/resize
     landing with Start earlier than GanttParityFixtures.CanDropBlackoutBefore
     (see that field's remarks for why 2026-03-05 against fixture task "fe3" is a
     clean, deterministic boundary) and counts every real ValidateDrop
     invocation into a sink (data-testid="candrop-call-count") so the E2E specs
     can assert the "0 calls when unset / 1 per snapped position / 0 during
     progress or create" call-frequency contract against the ACTUAL JS->.NET
     interop, not just BuildDragOptions' hasCanDrop flag (which is all bUnit
     could already assert without a real browser).
   - Event sinks (click/dateChange/progressChange/taskUpdate/taskCreate) mirror
     GanttV2Page.razor's — same rationale, same hidden <pre> convention. Also
     TasksChanged is bound (making this route "controlled" in GanttChart's
     controlled/uncontrolled discriminator sense) purely as a pass-through
     (always accepts what GanttChart pushes) so a created task's ids are observable
     in their own sink without ever vetoing/reverting an edit.

   Design spec Phase 3, T8 additions:
   - ?settingsMenu=1 -> renders a real GanttSettingsMenu in GanttChart.TrailingContent,
     two-way bound to the SAME fields already backing this page's own GanttChart
     parameters (settings-menu toggles are observable through the SAME live
     chart this page already renders, not a second/parallel instance) — lets an
     E2E spec drive a real settings-menu checkbox click and assert a live
     chart feature (e.g. ShowZoomControl's own ".lumeo-gantt-v3-zoom-control")
     actually flips.
   - ?barContextMenu=1 -> wires GanttChart.BarContextMenu to a minimal test menu
     (one item, data-testid="gantt-v3-context-menu-item", clicking it writes
     the right-clicked task's id into a sink) so an E2E spec can right-click a
     bar and assert the menu opens/positions/closes, and stays isolated from
     an in-flight drag (design spec Phase 3, T8, decision 4).
   - ?dragGhostTemplate=1 -> wires GanttChart.DragGhostTemplate to a distinctly
     testid'd/styled fragment (data-testid="gantt-v3-custom-ghost") so an E2E
     spec can assert the CUSTOM ghost (not the default bar clone) is what's
     actually visible during a live drag.

   ?rtl=1 (Codex round 3, P2 #7): wraps GanttChart in Lumeo's own DirectionProvider
   (the standard idiom every RTL-aware Lumeo component relies on — see
   DirectionProvider.razor's own remarks — sets dir="rtl" on a wrapping div,
   which every logical-CSS utility and gantt-v3.js's own RTL scrollLeft
   normalization resolve against) instead of a page-specific ad-hoc dir
   attribute, so this harness exercises the SAME code path a real RTL
   consumer would use.

   ?tree=0 (Codex round 4, P2 #2): every fixture on this page always passes a
   non-null GroupBy, which unconditionally satisfies GanttRowModel.
   DefaultShowTreePane's "GroupBy is set" branch regardless of whether any
   task actually HAS a GroupLabel — meaning the tree pane always renders here
   by default. The P2 #2 regression spec needs a like-for-like "without tree"
   comparison case (does scroll-centering math still land correctly when
   there's no tree-width offset to add at all), so this explicitly overrides
   GanttChart's ShowTreePane parameter to false when present.

   OnTaskClick sink (Codex round 5 review, Minor): the round-5 click-
   composition fix (P1 #1) only had bUnit coverage, which can't prove real
   DOM event bubbling — this host wires OnTaskClick to a plain
   data-testid="gantt-v3-last-clicked" element (AND the Phase-2 click
   event-sink JSON below, from the same handler) so an E2E spec can drive a
   REAL Playwright click on a rendered bar and assert the handler actually
   fired, closing that gap.

   data-testid="gantt-v3-toggle-direction" (Codex round 7 review, P2 #4):
   always wraps GanttChart in ONE DirectionProvider whose Direction is a mutable
   field (seeded from ?rtl=1, same as before) instead of only conditionally
   wrapping it — lets a spec flip direction on an ALREADY-MOUNTED chart via a
   real Blazor re-render (the same path a live DirectionProvider ancestor
   toggling Direction would take in a real app), rather than only ever
   observing direction fixed at page load. *@

<PageTitle>E2E - Gantt v3</PageTitle>

<div class="p-4" style="max-width: 1600px;">
    <h1 data-testid="gantt-e2e-title">Gantt v3 (parity fixture)</h1>
    <div data-testid="gantt-v3-last-clicked">@_lastClickedTaskId</div>
    <DirectionProvider Direction="@_direction">
        <GanttChart Tasks="@_tasks"
                TasksChanged="HandleTasksChanged"
                ViewMode="@_viewMode"
                ViewModeChanged="@(m => _viewMode = m)"
                Height="900px"
                GroupBy="@(t => t.GroupLabel ?? "")"
                ShowTreePane="@_showTreePaneOverride"
                BarColor="@GanttParityFixtures.GetBarColor"
                Readonly="@_readonly"
                AllowCreate="@_allowCreate"
                CanDrop="@(_useCanDrop ? CanDropHandler : null)"
                MarkOffDays="@_markOffDays"
                NowIndicator="@_nowIndicator"
                FirstDayOfWeek="@_firstDayOfWeek"
                ColorByGroup="@_colorByGroup"
                ShowOffscreenIndicators="@_showOffscreenIndicators"
                ShowZoomControl="@_showZoomControl"
                ShowSummaryBars="@_showSummaryBars"
                ShowRowCheckboxes="@_showRowCheckboxes"
                AllowRowReorder="@_allowRowReorder"
                ShowTaskMeta="@_showTaskMeta"
                OffDays="@_offDays"
                InfiniteScroll="@_infiniteScroll"
                OnTaskClick="HandleTaskClick"
                OnDateChange="HandleDateChange"
                OnProgressChange="HandleProgressChange"
                OnTaskUpdate="HandleTaskUpdate"
                OnTaskCreate="HandleTaskCreate"
                DragGhostTemplate="@(_showDragGhostTemplate ? DragGhostTemplateFragment : null)"
                BarContextMenu="@(_showBarContextMenu ? BarContextMenuFragment : null)"
                TrailingContent="@(_showSettingsMenu ? SettingsMenuFragment : null)"
                data-testid="gantt-v3-root" />
    </DirectionProvider>

    <pre data-testid="event-sink-click" style="display:none">@_lastClickJson</pre>
    <pre data-testid="event-sink-click-count" style="display:none">@_clickCount</pre>
    <pre data-testid="event-sink-datechange" style="display:none">@_lastDateChangeJson</pre>
    <pre data-testid="event-sink-progresschange" style="display:none">@_lastProgressChangeJson</pre>
    <pre data-testid="event-sink-taskupdate" style="display:none">@_lastTaskUpdateJson</pre>
    <pre data-testid="event-sink-taskcreate" style="display:none">@_lastTaskCreateJson</pre>
    <pre data-testid="event-sink-taskschanged" style="display:none">@_lastTasksChangedJson</pre>
    <pre data-testid="candrop-call-count" style="display:none">@_validateDropCallCount</pre>
    <pre data-testid="gantt-v3-context-menu-selected" style="display:none">@_lastContextMenuTaskId</pre>
    @* Bug fix (cx7b review): kept BELOW the chart, not above it - the visual
       snapshot suite screenshots a FIXED viewport clip from (0,0), so any
       harness control placed ABOVE the chart shifts the whole captured
       region down and stale-breaks every v3 baseline (exactly what adding
       this button above the chart did in round 7). A control added here in
       the future won't repeat that. *@
    <button type="button" data-testid="gantt-v3-toggle-direction" @onclick="ToggleDirection">Toggle direction</button>
</div>

@code {
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? Fixture { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? ViewMode { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? Readonly { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? AllowCreate { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "candrop")] public string? CanDropQuery { get; set; }
    // Codex P1 finding "Fail closed when CanDrop invocation rejects" —
    // ?candropthrow=1 (combined with ?candrop=1) makes the wired predicate
    // THROW unconditionally, simulating a consumer's CanDrop implementation
    // failing, so an E2E spec can drive a REAL drag against it and assert
    // gantt-v3.js's ValidateDrop rejection resolves to false (no commit),
    // not true (the pre-fix fail-open behavior) — this can only be proven
    // against the real interop round-trip; bUnit never executes gantt-v3.js.
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "candropthrow")] public string? CanDropThrowQuery { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? Rtl { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery] public string? Tree { get; set; }
    // Design spec Phase 3, T2 additions.
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "markOffDays")] public string? MarkOffDaysQuery { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "nowIndicator")] public string? NowIndicatorQuery { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "firstDayOfWeek")] public string? FirstDayOfWeekQuery { get; set; }
    // Design spec Phase 3, T7 additions.
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "colorByGroup")] public string? ColorByGroupQuery { get; set; }
    // ShowOffscreenIndicators defaults to true (GanttChart's own parameter
    // default) — this query flag exists to turn it OFF for the "no chip even
    // though a bar is offscreen" comparison spec, not to turn it on (already
    // the default).
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "showOffscreenIndicators")] public string? ShowOffscreenIndicatorsQuery { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "showZoomControl")] public string? ShowZoomControlQuery { get; set; }
    // 2026-08-10 shadcn alignment, G6 — tree row meta line ("date-range · N%").
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "showTaskMeta")] public string? ShowTaskMetaQuery { get; set; }
    // Design spec Phase 3, T9 — InfiniteScroll defaults to true (GanttChart's own
    // parameter default), so this query flag exists to turn it OFF for the
    // "byte-matches v2 fixed padding" parity spec, not to turn it on.
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "infiniteScroll")] public string? InfiniteScrollQuery { get; set; }
    // Design spec Phase 3, T8 additions — see this file's own header remarks.
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "settingsMenu")] public string? SettingsMenuQuery { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "barContextMenu")] public string? BarContextMenuQuery { get; set; }
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "dragGhostTemplate")] public string? DragGhostTemplateQuery { get; set; }

    private GanttViewMode _viewMode = GanttViewMode.Day;
    private List<GanttTask> _tasks = new();
    private bool _readonly;
    private bool _allowCreate;
    private bool _useCanDrop;
    private bool _throwInCanDrop;
    private int _validateDropCallCount;
    private bool? _showTreePaneOverride;
    private string _lastClickedTaskId = "";
    private LayoutDirection _direction = LayoutDirection.Ltr;
    private bool _markOffDays;
    private bool _nowIndicator;
    private DayOfWeek? _firstDayOfWeek;
    private bool _colorByGroup;
    private bool _showOffscreenIndicators = true;
    private bool _showZoomControl;
    private bool _showSummaryBars;
    private bool _showRowCheckboxes;
    private bool _allowRowReorder;
    private bool _showTaskMeta;
    private IReadOnlySet<DayOfWeek>? _offDays;
    private bool _infiniteScroll = true;

    // Design spec Phase 3, T8 additions.
    private bool _showSettingsMenu;
    private bool _showBarContextMenu;
    private bool _showDragGhostTemplate;
    private string? _lastContextMenuTaskId;

    private string? _lastClickJson;
    // Invocation-COUNT sink (Phase-1/Phase-2 reconciliation fix-round): the
    // sinks above only ever exposed the LAST payload's VALUE, which stays
    // identical whether OnTaskClick fired once or twice for the same click —
    // blind to the double-fire this round's own CRITICAL finding closed
    // (GanttBar's native onclick + GanttTimeline's JS-driven NotifyTaskClick
    // both invoking it). Counts every call so a spec can assert the exact
    // invocation count, not just the final value.
    private int _clickCount;
    private string? _lastDateChangeJson;
    private string? _lastProgressChangeJson;
    private string? _lastTaskUpdateJson;
    private string? _lastTaskCreateJson;
    private string? _lastTasksChangedJson;

    private void ToggleDirection() =>
        _direction = _direction == LayoutDirection.Ltr ? LayoutDirection.Rtl : LayoutDirection.Ltr;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _tasks = Fixture switch
        {
            "today" => GanttParityFixtures.TodayMarkerTasks(),
            "tall" => GanttParityFixtures.TallFixture(),
            "future" => GanttParityFixtures.FutureOnlyFixture(),
            "crossing" => GanttParityFixtures.CrossingDependencyFixture(),
            _ => GanttParityFixtures.SharedTasks(),
        };
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(ViewMode) && Enum.TryParse<GanttViewMode>(ViewMode, out var parsed))
            _viewMode = parsed;
        _readonly = Readonly == "1";
        _allowCreate = AllowCreate == "1";
        _useCanDrop = CanDropQuery == "1";
        _throwInCanDrop = CanDropThrowQuery == "1";
        if (Tree == "0") _showTreePaneOverride = false;
        if (Rtl == "1") _direction = LayoutDirection.Rtl;
        _markOffDays = MarkOffDaysQuery == "1";
        _nowIndicator = NowIndicatorQuery == "1";
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(FirstDayOfWeekQuery) && Enum.TryParse<DayOfWeek>(FirstDayOfWeekQuery, out var fdow))
            _firstDayOfWeek = fdow;
        _colorByGroup = ColorByGroupQuery == "1";
        if (ShowOffscreenIndicatorsQuery == "0") _showOffscreenIndicators = false;
        _showZoomControl = ShowZoomControlQuery == "1";
        _showTaskMeta = ShowTaskMetaQuery == "1";
        if (InfiniteScrollQuery == "0") _infiniteScroll = false;
        _showSettingsMenu = SettingsMenuQuery == "1";
        _showBarContextMenu = BarContextMenuQuery == "1";
        _showDragGhostTemplate = DragGhostTemplateQuery == "1";
    }

    // Design spec Phase 3, T8 — the real GanttSettingsMenu, two-way bound to
    // the SAME fields already backing this page's own <GanttChart> parameters
    // above (see this file's own header remarks) — a settings-menu toggle
    // click is observable through the identical live chart, not a second
    // instance. A plain attribute (not the <TrailingContent> child-content-
    // tag syntax) on <GanttChart> above, specifically so the ternary can still
    // supply a genuine null (no wrapper div at all on GanttNav's own side —
    // see GanttNav.razor's own "@if (TrailingContent is not null)" gate) when
    // ?settingsMenu=1 is absent, keeping every pre-T8 spec on this page
    // byte-identical.
    private RenderFragment SettingsMenuFragment =>
        @<GanttSettingsMenu @bind-ShowRowCheckboxes="_showRowCheckboxes"
                             @bind-ShowSummaryBars="_showSummaryBars"
                             @bind-ShowZoomControl="_showZoomControl"
                             @bind-ShowOffscreenIndicators="_showOffscreenIndicators"
                             @bind-InfiniteScroll="_infiniteScroll"
                             @bind-NowIndicator="_nowIndicator"
                             @bind-MarkOffDays="_markOffDays"
                             @bind-Readonly="_readonly"
                             @bind-AllowCreate="_allowCreate"
                             @bind-AllowRowReorder="_allowRowReorder"
                             @bind-FirstDayOfWeek="_firstDayOfWeek"
                             @bind-OffDays="_offDays"
                             @bind-ColorByGroup="_colorByGroup" />;

    // Design spec Phase 3, T8 — minimal test menu (one item) wired via
    // ?barContextMenu=1. Selecting it writes the right-clicked task's id into
    // a sink so an E2E spec can prove the resolved task matches the bar that
    // was actually right-clicked, not just "a menu opened".
    private RenderFragment<GanttTask> BarContextMenuFragment => task =>
        @<ContextMenuItem OnClick="@(() => HandleContextMenuItemSelect(task))" data-testid="gantt-v3-context-menu-item">
            Task: @task.Name
        </ContextMenuItem>;

    private void HandleContextMenuItemSelect(GanttTask task)
    {
        _lastContextMenuTaskId = task.Id;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    // Design spec Phase 3, T8 — a distinctly testid'd/styled ghost so an E2E
    // spec can assert the CUSTOM content (not the default bar clone) is what
    // actually renders during a live drag. Deliberately does NOT include a
    // ".lumeo-gantt-v3-bar-progress" element (see GanttBar.DragGhostTemplate's
    // own remarks — a progress drag simply skips the live fill repaint for a
    // custom template; this fixture intentionally exercises that path too).
    private static readonly RenderFragment<GanttTask> DragGhostTemplateFragment = task =>
        @<div class="absolute inset-0 rounded border-2 border-dashed border-destructive bg-destructive/20" data-testid="gantt-v3-custom-ghost"></div>;

    // Phase 2, T2/T3 (drag-parity sinks) + Codex round 5 review (real-DOM
    // click proof) share this one handler: sets the plain last-clicked-id
    // sink AND serializes the full task into the click event-sink JSON, so
    // a single Playwright click can drive both assertions.
    private Task HandleTaskClick(GanttTask t)
    {
        _lastClickedTaskId = t.Id;
        _lastClickJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(t);
        _clickCount++;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private Task HandleDateChange(GanttTask t)
    {
        _lastDateChangeJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(t);
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private Task HandleProgressChange(GanttTask t)
    {
        _lastProgressChangeJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(t);
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private GanttUpdateResult HandleTaskUpdate(GanttTaskUpdate u)
    {
        _lastTaskUpdateJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new { u.Task, Source = u.Source.ToString() });
        return true;
    }

    private Task HandleTaskCreate(GanttTaskUpdate u)
    {
        _lastTaskCreateJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new { u.Task, Source = u.Source.ToString() });
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private Task HandleTasksChanged(IEnumerable<GanttTask> tasks)
    {
        // Pass-through only: never vetoes, so this binding cannot alter behavior
        // for any route that doesn't exercise it (existing bar/arrow/nav specs
        // never fire a task edit, so _tasks here never actually changes for them).
        _tasks = tasks.ToList();
        _lastTasksChangedJson = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new { Count = _tasks.Count, Ids = _tasks.Select(t => t.Id) });
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private bool CanDropHandler(GanttTask task, GanttScheduleDropContext context)
    {
        // CanDrop is a plain Func, not an EventCallback — invoked synchronously
        // from GanttTimeline.ValidateDrop's [JSInvokable] method body, so unlike
        // the EventCallback-bound sinks above (whose receivers Blazor
        // auto-re-renders after invocation) mutating this page's own field here
        // does NOT by itself schedule a re-render of THIS component. Without an
        // explicit StateHasChanged, the candrop-call-count sink's <pre> would
        // never actually update in the DOM even though the field's value did —
        // invisible to a real browser/Playwright assertion.
        _validateDropCallCount++;
        StateHasChanged();
        // Codex P1 finding "Fail closed when CanDrop invocation rejects" —
        // simulates the predicate itself failing (see CanDropThrowQuery's
        // own remarks). Thrown AFTER the count/StateHasChanged above so the
        // call-count sink still proves the invocation actually happened —
        // a real failing predicate would ordinarily run its own logic
        // (including any counting side effects) before failing.
        if (_throwInCanDrop) throw new InvalidOperationException("simulated CanDrop predicate failure (E2E fixture)");
        var valid = context.ProposedStart >= GanttParityFixtures.CanDropBlackoutBefore;
        return valid;
    }
}
